{
  "id": "disk-full-docker",
  "title": "CUDA image build runs out of disk on ubuntu-latest after adding TensorRT and onnxruntime-gpu",
  "description": "PR #211 adds a TensorRT backend: requirements-gpu.txt gains onnxruntime-gpu and tensorrt-cu12 (which pulls the ~2 GB tensorrt_cu12_libs wheel). The requirements change invalidates the gha layer cache, so the build pulls and extracts the multi-GB nvidia/cuda cudnn-devel and cudnn-runtime bases and reinstalls torch + nvidia-* + TensorRT into /opt/venv. 'Runner resources' earlier in the log shows /dev/root at 80% with 15G free (/mnt has 66G free). The build dies copying the venv into the runtime stage: 'ERROR: failed to solve: failed to copy files: userspace copy failed: write .../libnvinfer_builder_resource.so.10.13.3: no space left on device'. build (cpu) passes and main history is green. Root cause is the hosted runner's disk, not the Python code: free space before building (remove preinstalled SDKs, prune), move Docker/buildkit data to /mnt, skip --load on PRs, slim the image, or use a larger runner. Distractor: apt's 'additional disk space will be used' line is normal output.",
